From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:07:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement ext-session-lock-v1

Let a lock client (swaylock, hyprlock, gtklock, ...) lock the session
with ext_session_lock_manager_v1:

- On lock, an opaque black actor covering the whole stage, with the
  lock surfaces on top, is kept above every other stage child, so no
  window, shell actor or drag icon is painted on any output; outputs
  added while locked are covered from their first frame. Direct
  scanout is inhibited so a fullscreen client cannot end up on a plane
  above it.
- locked is sent only once a frame painted with the blank has been
  presented on every output (or the outputs are powered off).
- Each lock surface is configured with its output's size, placed on
  that output and reconfigured when the output changes; subsurfaces of
  lock surfaces are shown with them. The commit_before_first_ack,
  null_buffer, dimensions_mismatch, invalid_serial, role,
  already_constructed, duplicate_output, invalid_destroy and
  invalid_unlock errors are enforced.
- A pinned Wayland event handler stays at the head of the handler list
  while locked, focuses only lock surfaces of the lock client (keyboard
  on the first lock surface, moved by clicking another one) and
  delivers events to them directly, bypassing popup grabs and drags
  that started before the lock. Lock surfaces have no window, so the
  pointer accepts them as focus. events.c skips window management and
  every keybinding but VT and keyboard layout switching.
- If the lock client goes away without unlock_and_destroy the session
  stays locked and blank, and a new lock client can lock it again and
  unlock it. A second lock while one is held gets finished.
- Flatpak-sandboxed clients are not offered the global.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
